IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cla2-common`

-- Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) -- baseline-2026-11: Part 2A, child sexual abuse actions (ss 15A-15L).
--
-- SEAT. The person who was sexually abused as a child and brings, or may bring, a child sexual abuse action. Every
-- question is asked as that person would ask it; every input is a fact that person (or their lawyer) could state.
-- The court, the Minister and the institution are not seats.
--
-- Borrowed terms, asked as facts: "child sexual abuse", "child sexual abuse action" and "child sexual abuse cause of action"
-- have "the meaning given in the Limitation Act 2005 section 6A(1)" (s 15A); "costs determination" and "law practice" are
-- the Legal Profession Uniform Law's (s 15L(1)). Judgments handed to the court ("substantially the same", whether the court
-- is satisfied what share of a payment was for the abuse) are inputs.
--
-- Out: s 15J (a declaration for the Corporations Act 2001 (Cth) s 5G, which changes nothing for the person), s 15M (the
-- Minister's review), and the regulation-making power in s 15G(5)-(7) except as a fact ("a regulation names ...").
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Part 2A -- child sexual abuse actions`

§§ `ss 15A, 15B, 15D, 15F-15I -- whom I can sue when the institution was unincorporated`

-- s 15A: "institution means an entity (other than the Crown), organised for some purpose or work, that exercises or
-- exercised care, supervision or authority over children".
--
-- ss 15F, 15G: how the institution as it is now relates to the institution at the time the cause of action accrued.
--   s 15F(1): "it is sufficient that an institution (as it is currently) is substantially the same as it was";
--   s 15F(2): it is substantially the same "if the class or type of member and the primary purposes or work ... are
--             substantially the same"; (3): whatever changes of name, structure, incorporation or area;
--   s 15G(1)-(4): if no current institution is the same or substantially the same, "the relevant successor" is taken to be
--             the same institution: one that some or all of the earlier institution merged into, one formed by a merger of
--             some or all of it with others, or the remainder after part of it left (3); or a chain of such links, or of
--             "substantially the same" links (4);
--   s 15G(5), (7): a regulation may name the relevant successor, and it "prevail[s] over subsections (2) to (4)".
DECLARE `How the institution now relates to the one at the time of the abuse` IS ONE OF
    `it is the same institution`
    `its class of members and its primary purposes or work are substantially the same (s 15F(2))`
    `the court finds it substantially the same on other grounds (s 15F(1))`
    `none is the same: some or all of the earlier institution merged into it (s 15G(3)(a))`
    `none is the same: some or all of the earlier institution merged with others to form it (s 15G(3)(b))`
    `none is the same: it is what remains after part of the earlier institution left (s 15G(3)(c))`
    `none is the same: it descends through a chain of mergers, remainders or substantially-the-same links (s 15G(2)(b), (4))`
    `none is the same: a regulation names it as the relevant successor (s 15G(5))`
    `no institution now is the same, substantially the same or a successor`

DECLARE `Whom I can sue under Part 2A` IS ONE OF
    `the current holder of the office, in the name of the office (s 15B)`
    `the current head of the institution, as the current office holder (ss 15B, 15H(2))`
    `the institution itself, which is now incorporated (s 15D)`
    `Part 2A is not needed: the office holder still holds the office, and is sued as the general law allows`
    `Part 2A gives no one to sue on these facts`

GIVEN r IS A `How the institution now relates to the one at the time of the abuse`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is the same or substantially the same (s 15F)` IF
       r EQUALS `it is the same institution`
    OR r EQUALS `its class of members and its primary purposes or work are substantially the same (s 15F(2))`
    OR r EQUALS `the court finds it substantially the same on other grounds (s 15F(1))`

-- s 15G(1): the relevant successor "is taken to be the same institution as the earlier institution for the purposes of this
-- Division". A regulation naming a different institution prevails (s 15G(7)(a)); the encoder reads one successor only.
GIVEN r IS A `How the institution now relates to the one at the time of the abuse`, `another is named` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is the relevant successor (s 15G)` IF
       r EQUALS `none is the same: a regulation names it as the relevant successor (s 15G(5))`
    OR (    (   r EQUALS `none is the same: some or all of the earlier institution merged into it (s 15G(3)(a))`
             OR r EQUALS `none is the same: some or all of the earlier institution merged with others to form it (s 15G(3)(b))`
             OR r EQUALS `none is the same: it is what remains after part of the earlier institution left (s 15G(3)(c))`
             OR r EQUALS `none is the same: it descends through a chain of mergers, remainders or substantially-the-same links (s 15G(2)(b), (4))`)
        AND (NOT `another is named`))

-- ss 15B(1), 15D(1), with s 15I: "if a child sexual abuse cause of action does not accrue at the time of the act or omission
-- giving rise to the cause of action, the cause of action is taken to have accrued at the time of the act or omission". So
-- "at the time of the accrual of the cause of action" (ss 15B(1)(c), 15D(1)(c)) is always the time of the abuse, and the
-- inputs ask about that time. ss 15B(4), 15D(4): the sections apply "regardless of when" the abuse happened or the cause of
-- action accrued, so no date is asked.
--
-- s 15B(1): "(a) a person was subjected to child sexual abuse by a person associated with an institution; and (b) the person
-- has or had a child sexual abuse cause of action against the holder of an office of authority in the institution ...
-- founded on the responsibility of the office holder for the associated person and for the institution generally; and (c) at
-- the time of the accrual ..., the institution -- (i) exercised care, supervision or authority over children; and (ii) was
-- not incorporated; and (d) the institution is currently not incorporated; and (e) the office holder no longer holds the
-- office; and (f) the person would be able to maintain an action on the cause of action if the office holder continued to
-- hold the office." (2): the action "may be commenced against the current holder of the office ... in the name of the
-- office". (3): the office holder's liability "is taken to be held by the current office holder".
-- s 15H(1): the office suffices if it is "substantially the same"; (2): if no current office is, "but there is continuity of
-- the institution, the current head of the institution is taken to be the current office holder"; (4): continuity means the
-- institution is the same as at accrual (with s 15F(1), substantially the same) or the same under s 15G.
-- s 15D(1): (a)-(c) as s 15B, "(d) the institution is currently incorporated; and (e) the person is able to maintain an
-- action on the cause of action or would be able to do so if the office holder continued to hold the office." (2): the
-- action "may be commenced against the institution"; (3): it holds the office holder's liability.
@export Whom can I sue under Part 2A of the Civil Liability Act for child sexual abuse in an institution that was not incorporated at the time (ss 15A, 15B, 15D, 15F-15I)?
GIVEN
    `I was sexually abused as a child by a person associated with the institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you subjected to child sexual abuse (as the Limitation Act 2005 s 6A defines it) by a person associated with the institution?
    `I have or had a cause of action against an office holder for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have, or did you have, a child sexual abuse cause of action against the holder of an office of authority in the institution, founded on their responsibility for the abuser and for the institution generally?
    `the institution is the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body the State (the Crown) itself, rather than an organisation such as a church, school, club or charity?
    `at the time it exercised care, supervision or authority over children` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of the abuse, did the institution exercise care, supervision or authority over children?
    `at the time it was incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of the abuse, was the institution incorporated (a company, an incorporated association or another body corporate)?
    `it is incorporated now` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the institution as it is now (or its successor) incorporated today?
    `how it relates now` IS A `How the institution now relates to the one at the time of the abuse` @desc How does the institution as it is now relate to the institution at the time of the abuse?
    `a regulation names a different institution as the successor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a regulation under s 15G(5) name some other institution as the relevant successor? Answer no if you know of none.
    `the office is substantially the same now` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there an office in the institution now that is the same, or substantially the same, as the office of authority the person responsible held?
    `the office holder still holds the office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person who held that office of authority at the time still hold it?
    `I could sue if they still held the office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you be able to maintain an action on your cause of action if that office holder still held the office (for example, it is not time-barred or already settled)?
GIVETH A `Whom I can sue under Part 2A`
DECIDE `Whom can I sue for abuse in an institution that was unincorporated` IS
    IF      (NOT `I was sexually abused as a child by a person associated with the institution`)
         OR (NOT `I have or had a cause of action against an office holder for it`)
         OR `the institution is the Crown`
         OR (NOT `at the time it exercised care, supervision or authority over children`)
         OR `at the time it was incorporated`
         OR (NOT `there is continuity of the institution`)
         OR (NOT `I could sue if they still held the office`)
    THEN `Part 2A gives no one to sue on these facts`
    ELSE IF `it is incorporated now`
         THEN `the institution itself, which is now incorporated (s 15D)`
         ELSE IF `the office holder still holds the office`
              THEN `Part 2A is not needed: the office holder still holds the office, and is sued as the general law allows`
              ELSE IF `the office is substantially the same now`
                   THEN `the current holder of the office, in the name of the office (s 15B)`
                   ELSE `the current head of the institution, as the current office holder (ss 15B, 15H(2))`
    WHERE
        `there is continuity of the institution` MEANS
               `it is the same or substantially the same (s 15F)` `how it relates now`
            OR `it is the relevant successor (s 15G)` `how it relates now` `a regulation names a different institution as the successor`

§§ `ss 15C, 15E -- what my judgment or settlement can be paid from`

DECLARE `Who is liable to me under the judgment or settlement` IS ONE OF
    `the holder of an office of authority in the institution, on a cause of action of the s 15B(1)(b) type`
    `an institution`
    `someone else`

-- s 15C(1), (2): if "a holder of an office of authority in an institution has a liability under a judgment in or settlement
-- of an action on a child sexual abuse cause of action of the type described in section 15B(1)(b)", the holder "may satisfy
-- the liability out of assets held by or for the office or the institution, including assets of a trust (whether or not a
-- charitable trust)". s 15E(1), (2): if "an institution has a liability under a judgment in or settlement of a child sexual
-- abuse action", it "may satisfy the liability out of assets held by or for the institution, including assets of a trust".
-- ss 15C(5), 15E(4): despite any law, trust term or duty. ss 15C(7), 15E(5): neither section applies "in relation to a
-- judgment in or settlement of a child sexual abuse action given or reached before" 1 July 2018. Outside the sections the
-- general law decides: NOTHING.
@export Can my judgment or settlement for child sexual abuse be paid out of the institution's assets, including trust assets (ss 15C, 15E)?
GIVEN
    `who is liable` IS A `Who is liable to me under the judgment or settlement` @desc Who must pay you under the judgment or settlement: an office holder in the institution (sued for their responsibility for the abuser and the institution), the institution itself, or someone else?
    `the date of the judgment or settlement` IS A DATE @desc The date the judgment was given or the settlement was reached
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my judgment or settlement be paid from the institution's assets and trusts` IS
    IF `is before Part 2A commenced` `the date of the judgment or settlement`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `who is liable`
         WHEN `someone else` THEN NOTHING
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 15C(3): "However, personal assets of the holder of the office cannot be used to satisfy the liability." (6): "despite any
-- written or other law, including the Civil Judgments Enforcement Act 2004". A flat negative: JUST FALSE where s 15C applies;
-- NOTHING where it does not (an institution's liability, someone else's, or a judgment or settlement before 1 July 2018).
@export Can the office holder's own personal assets be used to pay my judgment or settlement for child sexual abuse (s 15C(3))?
GIVEN
    `who is liable` IS A `Who is liable to me under the judgment or settlement` @desc Who must pay you under the judgment or settlement: an office holder in the institution (sued for their responsibility for the abuser and the institution), the institution itself, or someone else?
    `the date of the judgment or settlement` IS A DATE @desc The date the judgment was given or the settlement was reached
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the office holder's personal assets be used to pay me` IS
    IF `is before Part 2A commenced` `the date of the judgment or settlement`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `who is liable`
         WHEN `the holder of an office of authority in the institution, on a cause of action of the s 15B(1)(b) type` THEN JUST FALSE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 15K -- earlier redress payments deducted from my damages`

-- s 15K(1): "compensation payment, made in respect of a person -- (a) means a payment made in respect of the person by way of
-- compensation or redress (including an ex gratia payment) for child sexual abuse of the person; but (b) does not include an
-- amount paid under a judgment in or settlement of a child sexual abuse action."
-- (2): the court "must deduct an amount equal to the amount of any compensation payment made in respect of the person for the
-- child sexual abuse the subject of the action". (3): "only to the extent to which the compensation payment is for that child
-- sexual abuse". (4): "If the court is not satisfied as to the extent ..., the court must deduct an amount equal to 50% of
-- the payment." (5): the court may still "take into account an amount paid under a judgment in or settlement of a previous
-- child sexual abuse action" -- so for such an amount s 15K sets no deduction and the answer is NOTHING.
-- One payment is one case; for several, add the deductions.
@export How much of an earlier compensation or redress payment must be deducted from my damages for child sexual abuse (s 15K)?
GIVEN
    `it was paid for child sexual abuse of me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the payment made to you, or for you, as compensation or redress for child sexual abuse of you (an ex gratia or redress scheme payment counts)?
    `it was paid under a judgment or settlement of a child sexual abuse action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the payment made under a court judgment in, or a settlement of, an earlier child sexual abuse action?
    `the payment` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of the payment, in dollars
    `the court is satisfied how much was for this abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied how much of the payment was for the abuse your present action is about?
    `the part for this abuse` IS A NUMBER @desc If the court is satisfied, the part of the payment (in dollars) that was for the abuse your present action is about
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of an earlier payment is deducted from my damages` IS
    IF `it was paid under a judgment or settlement of a child sexual abuse action`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF (NOT `it was paid for child sexual abuse of me`)
         THEN JUST 0
         ELSE IF `the court is satisfied how much was for this abuse`
              THEN JUST `the part for this abuse`
              ELSE JUST (`the payment` TIMES (50%))

-- The award after the deduction. s 15K does not say what happens if the deduction exceeds the damages; the encoder reads that
-- nothing is awarded and nothing is owed back (fork F5 in NOTES.md).
@export How much will I be awarded for child sexual abuse after an earlier compensation or redress payment is deducted (s 15K)?
GIVEN
    `the damages assessed` IS A NUMBER @desc The damages the court assesses for your action before any deduction, in dollars
    `it was paid for child sexual abuse of me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the payment made to you, or for you, as compensation or redress for child sexual abuse of you (an ex gratia or redress scheme payment counts)?
    `it was paid under a judgment or settlement of a child sexual abuse action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the payment made under a court judgment in, or a settlement of, an earlier child sexual abuse action?
    `the payment` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of the payment, in dollars
    `the court is satisfied how much was for this abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied how much of the payment was for the abuse your present action is about?
    `the part for this abuse` IS A NUMBER @desc If the court is satisfied, the part of the payment (in dollars) that was for the abuse your present action is about
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much will I be awarded after the deduction` IS
    CONSIDER `How much of an earlier payment is deducted from my damages` `it was paid for child sexual abuse of me` `it was paid under a judgment or settlement of a child sexual abuse action` `the payment` `the court is satisfied how much was for this abuse` `the part for this abuse`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST d THEN JUST (`the damages less` d)
    WHERE
        GIVEN d IS A NUMBER
        `the damages less` d MEANS
            IF d AT LEAST `the damages assessed`
            THEN 0
            ELSE `the damages assessed` MINUS d

§§ `s 15L -- the cap on my lawyers' fees`

-- s 15L(2): "An agreement must not be made for a law practice to receive, for appearing for or acting on behalf of a person
-- in a child sexual abuse action, any greater reward than is provided for by any costs determination that is in force."
-- (3): "An agreement is void, and any money paid under the agreement is recoverable by the person who paid the money, if the
-- agreement -- (a) is made contrary to this section; or (b) would have been contrary to this section if it had been made after
-- the commencement of" Part 2A (1 July 2018). (4): (3) "does not affect the operation of an agreement so far as it relates to
-- services provided before" 1 July 2018 "and does not apply in relation to any money paid or payable in respect of services
-- so provided".
-- Whether a costs determination (made under the Legal Profession Uniform Law Application Act 2022 s 133) is in force, and the
-- reward it provides, are facts. The prohibition has no deadline and is addressed to the parties to the agreement; it is
-- encoded as its consequence for the client, not as a DEONTIC rule.
@export Is my fee agreement with my lawyers for a child sexual abuse action void because it gives them more than the costs determination allows (s 15L)?
GIVEN
    `a costs determination is in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a legal costs determination in force that covers acting for a person in a child sexual abuse action?
    `the most it allows` IS A NUMBER @desc The most reward, in dollars, the costs determination provides for the work your agreement covers
    `the reward the agreement gives` IS A NUMBER @desc The reward, in dollars, your agreement gives the law practice for appearing or acting for you in the action
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my fee agreement void` IS
    IF `a costs determination is in force` AND `the reward the agreement gives` GREATER THAN `the most it allows`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 15L(3), (4): if the agreement is void, all the money paid under it is recoverable by whoever paid it -- not just the
-- excess over the determination -- except money paid or payable for services provided before 1 July 2018.
@export How much of what I paid my lawyers under a fee agreement for a child sexual abuse action can I get back (s 15L)?
GIVEN
    `a costs determination is in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a legal costs determination in force that covers acting for a person in a child sexual abuse action?
    `the most it allows` IS A NUMBER @desc The most reward, in dollars, the costs determination provides for the work your agreement covers
    `the reward the agreement gives` IS A NUMBER @desc The reward, in dollars, your agreement gives the law practice for appearing or acting for you in the action
    `what I paid for services from 1 July 2018` IS A NUMBER @desc How much you yourself paid under the agreement, in dollars, for services provided on or after 1 July 2018
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my legal fees can I get back` IS
    IF `Is my fee agreement void` `a costs determination is in force` `the most it allows` `the reward the agreement gives` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST `what I paid for services from 1 July 2018`
    ELSE JUST 0
